# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...except the template, which documents every variable the app needs
# and holds only placeholders. README and DEPLOYMENT.md both point at it.
!.env.example

# Installed agent skills. Treated like node_modules: the content is fetched,
# not authored here, and skills-lock.json pins the source and hash so
# `npx skills add supabase/agent-skills` reproduces it exactly.
#
# .claude/skills is a symlink mirror of .agents/skills. Windows checkouts have
# core.symlinks=false, so git follows the links and would commit a second copy
# of all 40 files that can then drift from the first. Both spellings are needed:
# the trailing slash ignores a real directory, the bare name ignores the symlink.
.agents/
.claude/skills/
.claude/skills

# build output: derived from PROJECT_STATUS.html by scripts/build-status-artifact.mjs
build/

# build output: copied from PROJECT_STATUS.html by scripts/copy-status.mjs
public/status.html

# supabase cli scratch
supabase/.temp

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# database exports
# scripts/db-export.mjs reads with the service-role key, so its output is every
# document, question and answer in the platform, in plaintext. Never commit it.
/db/export/
